  "note": "Mississippi elects county offices in odd years, so this November 2026 ballot is federal and judicial. Shown are the contests every Jackson County voter votes on, from the county's official sample ballot: Court of Appeals District 5 (all of Jackson County), 16th Chancery District and 19th Circuit District (elected districtwide; under the 2025 redistricting laws the 19th Circuit is Jackson County alone starting in 2027), and County Court Judge Places 1 and 2. Not shown because they depend on your district: Election Commissioner District 4, Jackson County School Board District 4, Moss Point School District trustees 2 and 3, and the Ocean Springs School District board seat. No Pascagoula city offices are on this ballot. Incumbent flags come from the Mississippi Judiciary's judge rosters; County Court judges are not marked because no official roster was checked. Check your official sample ballot.",
